    <!-- Welcome -->
    <string name="welcome_1_title">Race the one who did it yesterday</string>
    <string name="welcome_1_text">Every task you do again and again becomes a discipline: the morning, the kitchen after dinner, a plank. Start the clock, and in the next lane runs a ghost: you, the last time or at your best. Split the sections, see where you\'re ahead, and finish.</string>
    <string name="welcome_2_title">Medals, and the Games</string>
    <string name="welcome_2_text">The first three heats are qualifying: a standard has to exist. After that, every heat among your top three gets a medal, and the best of all is the record. Every four weeks the Games close with a medal table, kept by parts of life instead of nations. Rushed doesn\'t count: speed is never the point on its own.</string>
    <string name="welcome_3_title">Your first disciplines</string>
    <string name="welcome_3_text">Pick a few to begin with. You can rename them, add sections and make your own at any time.</string>
    <string name="welcome_start">Open the Games</string>

